# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for tonight's four-card window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/serve-3 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN.
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. Every value is final.
# ORDER.txt says the order, each job's image, its stop rule and its minutes. The image is tp4-serve-3 throughout: T1 builds it, the
# later jobs serve it, and a commit after T1's tag needs a new tag and every later job the new one.
# T1: build tp4-serve-3 and smoke the PRODUCTION configuration: c2-packed-tp4, the traffic profile, audits ON, the tail caps ON
# (QWEN_FAST_BUDGET_CAP=1) and the sequential-step watchdog at 120 s (QWEN_FAST_SEQ_DEADLINE_S). The image's default diagnostics
# (memory ledger, carry log, phase log, sequential publish log) are as in v166. Preconditions: production is down with the user's
# go-ahead and the rig's disk is checked before the build.
# The test list is v166's SS list unchanged and in its order, then concurrent4_solo (each concurrent4 prompt alone at 800 tokens:
# this image's own full-text references for the four users) and the two coding-text concurrency tests, which come after the
# like-for-like part so its order and clock are v166's. The smoke script runs concurrent4_solo after alive_after_drop.
# READ the log, not only the verdict:
#  - '[PINDIAG] packed-any admission passed:' and NO UNQUALIFIED line; the prefill warm before Metal's unsafe-allocation warning;
#    no late prefill program; c2_smoke_check clean with audit_mismatches 0; no watchdog or replay-deadline exit.
#  - caps: every decode step with cached >= 2 has total = 16 x cached; one '[PINDIAG] packed budget cap' line per capped commit with
#    emitted <= remaining; every concurrent user completion_tokens == 800 and finish=length; no rows=1 or rows=2 SEQ-PUBLISH step.
#  - exactness: every concurrent4 user's content and reasoning hashes equal its concurrent4_solo run; tokens equal v166's at every
#    position both logs record; the first 300 characters of every text equal v166's.
#  - speed, like-for-like with v166: coding, long_real_text, concurrent4 mean and concurrent4_steady mean each no more than 5% below
#    v166's (35.84, 34.59, 15.79, 17.24 tok/s); report the live-4 round median, tail seconds and storm seconds beside v166's.
# Duration (estimate): 45 min. Stop rule: a hang on this configuration stops the window and goes to T6; a divergence or a vLLM
# refusal caused by the caps skips T2 and continues with T3 and T5.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=status reset build smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-3
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,long_real_text,concurrent4,concurrent4_steady,steady_resend,tool_call,stream_tool_call,stream_reasoning,refused_n2,alive_after_refusal,stream_dropped,alive_after_drop,concurrent4_solo,concurrent4_code,concurrent4_code_equal
